    "visual_differences": {
      "all": "Existing Godot font, spacing, border and HUD alignment differ slightly. Fixtures use Saturday or Sunday in place of the masters' Thursday and Friday.",
      "c17, c24, c26–c28": "Existing map rendering has different label outlines and gate marker. Toolbar gaps and widths follow the installed fonts and available actions.",
      "c18–c23, c25": "Locked placeholder direction: simple Godot buildings and oven with named capsules, viewed from inside the square to show Faris running. The prototype uses a dressed street from a different angle. Panel typography, line breaks, padding and widths of the compact buttons differ slightly.",
      "c18–c19, c26–c28": "Current HUD shows the weekday without the later Hijri date. Journal, The dry fountain, Feed the poor, Talk to Salma and Read the calligraphy are later features visible in c26–c28. The board bar is narrower, and c27–c28 fit their controls on a single line.",
      "c24": "The current prayer row wraps above the toolbar to fit Pray Asr here and the available Make up Dhuhr action. The bread grab actions are gone.",
      "c25": "The build keeps the live 16:10 after the lie. The master uses a 10:00 setup state.",
      "c28": "The later-day fixture shows a pending Fajr make-up. The master shows Dhuhr make-up."
    },
